    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** IoT connectivity connections grew 11%, while IoT Solutions revenue declined, painting a mixed demand picture. Free cash flow generation improved, underscoring better cash conversion. The dominant shift is the definitive agreement to be acquired by Searchlight Capital and Abry Partners, which will take KORE private and overshadows standalone operating trends. (A news item about KORE Digital’s AI data center is unrelated to the listed IoT hyperscaler and is excluded.)\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management opted for a take-private transaction at a substantial premium, signaling a belief that the public market undervalued the business. Q1 results included transaction-related costs that inflated net losses, yet the team emphasized free cash flow growth and cost discipline. A recent IoT asset tracking award highlights continued product recognition. Execution is now centered on closing the acquisition.",
